# FE4 Oracle read-only plugin

The plugin may only use the read-only user from initial setup.
It may only connect to FE4.
It must never log in with any other user obtained from the codebase, config files, or any other source.
It must never execute UPDATE, DELETE, or INSERT — SELECT (and `WITH ... SELECT`) only.

## Hard boundaries

- Use **only** the `fe4-oracle-readonly` MCP server. Never use `oracle-sqlcl`, `sqlcl`, or any other Oracle MCP.
- Never pass username, password, host, DSN, or connection name into a tool. Those are pinned in the plugin.
- Never read `web.config`, `appsettings`, connection strings, or secrets from the repo in order to connect.
- Never suggest `conn -savepwd`, `sqlplus`, or `sqlcl` from the agent shell.
- When a hook blocks a call: report the block and stop. Do not retry, reword, split the statement, or switch tools to get the same effect.
- If a write is genuinely required, tell the user to run it themselves outside the agent.

## Allowed

- A single `SELECT` or `WITH ... SELECT` via `sql_run`
- `session_info` and `schema_information` on the pinned session

## Query style

Prefer bind variables (`:param_name`), ANSI joins, and `FETCH FIRST n ROWS ONLY` when exploring.
